1
00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:02,660
Wealth, Fame, Power.

2
00:00:02,940 --> 00:00:04,597
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

3
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:07,197
attained this and everything
else the world had to offer,

4
00:00:07,280 --> 00:00:10,456
and his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

5
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:11,975
You want my treasure?

6
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:13,420
You can have it.

7
00:00:13,640 --> 00:00:16,640
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

8
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:19,060
Now you just have to find it.

9
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:24,217
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuit

10
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:26,737
of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine.

11
00:00:26,820 --> 00:00:29,517
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era.

12
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:34,980
Come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

13
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:40,440
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

14
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:42,700
One piece.

15
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,577
Compass left behind,
it'll only slow us down.

16
00:00:52,660 --> 00:00:58,417
Your heart will be your guide,
raise the sails and take the helm.

17
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:04,117
That legendary place that
the end of the map reveals.

18
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:10,137
Is only legendary until
someone proves it real.

19
00:01:10,220 --> 00:01:14,497
Through it all, through
all the trouble and times.

20
00:01:14,580 --> 00:01:16,817
Through the heartache
and through the pain.

21
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:21,477
Know that I will be there to stand by you.

22
00:01:21,560 --> 00:01:24,240
Just like I know you'll stand by me.

23
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:30,580
So come aboard and bring along
All your hopes and dreams.

24
00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:36,000
Together we will find everything
That we're looking for.

25
00:01:37,160 --> 00:01:39,677
There's always room for you.

26
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:42,460
If you wanna be my friend.

27
00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:46,800
We are, we are on a cruise.

28
00:01:48,380 --> 00:01:49,720
We are.

29
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:56,317
Wait, he just...

30
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:58,740
He just broke Captain Kudo's cat claw.

31
00:02:02,060 --> 00:02:05,020
That leaves only five more
of those weird swords.

32
00:02:08,520 --> 00:02:09,620
Don't worry, guys.

33
00:02:09,820 --> 00:02:11,237
He can still fight plenty.

34
00:02:11,320 --> 00:02:14,200
Yeah, he still has another
claw. You can do it!

35
00:02:14,300 --> 00:02:16,476
Rip that Katorea shrimp, Captain Kaido!

36
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:18,447
Don't use that name anymore.

37
00:02:18,540 --> 00:02:19,917
He doesn't like it, remember?

38
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:23,317
I think in this village his
name is Kla-ha... something.

39
00:02:23,400 --> 00:02:28,140
Kla-ha something! Yeah! Kla-ha
something! Get him! Good!

40
00:02:30,100 --> 00:02:31,860
Shut your mouths!

41
00:02:32,180 --> 00:02:33,120
All of you!

42
00:02:39,380 --> 00:02:41,640
Come out, you brats!

43
00:02:42,380 --> 00:02:43,840
I know you're hiding!

44
00:02:44,160 --> 00:02:45,540
Give yourselves up!

45
00:02:48,820 --> 00:02:51,232
Come over here and we'll take you to her!

46
00:02:51,340 --> 00:02:52,860
Just don't kill us!

47
00:02:54,560 --> 00:02:56,280
Do you think I'm stupid?

48
00:02:56,580 --> 00:02:59,540
I won't fall for that, you silly rugrats.

49
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:03,700
Oh, damn it.

50
00:03:05,420 --> 00:03:07,600
We got him! No!

51
00:03:10,640 --> 00:03:12,120
Pepper attack!

52
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:24,360
Achoo!

53
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:47,480
End of the line, hypnotist!

54
00:03:53,740 --> 00:03:57,093
Looks like you bit off a little
more than you could chew.

55
00:03:57,300 --> 00:03:58,130
No!

56
00:03:58,360 --> 00:03:59,740
We failed!

57
00:04:00,080 --> 00:04:04,440
Real pirates don't take kindly to
being mocked by the likes of you!

58
00:04:07,120 --> 00:04:07,950
Onion!

59
00:04:08,300 --> 00:04:09,800
You pretend, pirates.

60
00:04:09,900 --> 00:04:12,253
Sure got in over your heads, didn't you?

61
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:18,460
Rich girl, I know you're here. Listen!

62
00:04:18,920 --> 00:04:22,497
Unless you show yourself, I'll
execute these three little lambs.

63
00:04:22,580 --> 00:04:26,220
and I will make sure to do
it in a most painful fashion.

64
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:29,280
Do not doubt my skill at such a task.

65
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:39,160
There you are.

66
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:42,660
Miss Kaya, run for your life!

67
00:04:43,320 --> 00:04:44,150
Hey.

68
00:04:44,233 --> 00:04:45,886
Yeah, that's them, all right.

69
00:04:46,220 --> 00:04:47,514
They're the other way.

70
00:04:48,860 --> 00:04:50,797
Soon enough, I'll deal with you.

71
00:04:50,880 --> 00:04:54,417
In the only appropriate
manner, extermination.

72
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:56,797
I'll also kill that full jungle.

73
00:04:56,880 --> 00:05:00,057
But why kill us, captain?

74
00:05:00,140 --> 00:05:02,437
Come on, please don't
talk around like that.

75
00:05:02,520 --> 00:05:06,277
Captain, guru, it's still not too late
for us to attack the village, right?

76
00:05:06,360 --> 00:05:07,190
Yeah.

77
00:05:07,273 --> 00:05:08,977
And if captain jungle gets her to write,

78
00:05:09,060 --> 00:05:11,257
her will, then your plan
should still work perfectly.

79
00:05:11,340 --> 00:05:16,617
This plan is no longer
any of your concern.

80
00:05:16,700 --> 00:05:21,157
When all of you are dead, this village
will know who to blame for this atrocity.

81
00:05:21,240 --> 00:05:27,137
I never intended to let any of you
mongrels leave this village alive.

82
00:05:27,220 --> 00:05:28,717
No one.

83
00:05:28,800 --> 00:05:29,777
No one.

84
00:05:29,860 --> 00:05:33,097
Who knows my true identity can be
allowed to live to tell about it.

85
00:05:33,180 --> 00:05:35,157
No way.

86
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:39,769
You had already planned to kill every
last one of us from the very beginning.

87
00:05:41,520 --> 00:05:42,600
That's right.

88
00:05:43,520 --> 00:05:47,237
Three years ago, I planned
to erase Captain Kaido.

89
00:05:47,320 --> 00:05:50,817
And every last person who ever knew him.

90
00:05:50,900 --> 00:05:53,760
It's all part of my plan.

91
00:05:56,360 --> 00:05:57,937
You guys are dumb.

92
00:05:58,020 --> 00:06:00,780
You're the most Uncle pirates I know.

93
00:06:01,640 --> 00:06:03,220
We're Uncle, huh?

94
00:06:03,660 --> 00:06:05,697
Pirates are nothing more than savages.

95
00:06:05,780 --> 00:06:08,580
Incapable of rising above
their animal nature!

96
00:06:09,260 --> 00:06:12,436
Without my plans, what could
they possibly accomplish?

97
00:06:12,600 --> 00:06:14,140
A crew is nothing to me.

98
00:06:14,300 --> 00:06:16,300
They are simply a means to an end.

99
00:06:17,300 --> 00:06:20,241
Crew members are just pawns
in the captain's game.

100
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:24,179
Whether my men live or die
is up to me and me alone.

101
00:06:24,520 --> 00:06:26,837
If I tell them to fight, they will fight.

102
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:29,777
And if I order them to
die, they had better do it.

103
00:06:29,860 --> 00:06:32,360
They know the punishment for disobedience.

104
00:06:34,760 --> 00:06:36,457
This is how pirates are!

105
00:06:36,540 --> 00:06:39,420
Don't you dare talk down to me, boy!

106
00:06:45,780 --> 00:06:46,610
You know,

107
00:06:46,693 --> 00:06:51,180
no matter how many hundreds or thousands
of men follow you as their captain,

108
00:06:51,940 --> 00:06:54,460
you will never be as good as Usopp.

109
00:06:57,340 --> 00:06:58,380
You fool.

110
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:04,700
Are you saying that I am inferior to a kid
pretending to be a pirate? That's right.

111
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:08,740
Well, aren't you funny?

112
00:07:09,100 --> 00:07:13,159
Don't get all cocky just because
you snapped off one of my cat claws.

113
00:07:13,320 --> 00:07:15,720
How exactly is he better than me?

114
00:07:16,360 --> 00:07:17,440
Let's hear it.

115
00:07:22,260 --> 00:07:23,495
Cause he's got heart.

116
00:07:24,320 --> 00:07:25,340
He's got what?

117
00:07:26,700 --> 00:07:30,300
A guy like you doesn't
know what a true pirate is.

118
00:07:43,140 --> 00:07:43,970
Impossible!

119
00:07:44,220 --> 00:07:46,514
He kept up with the pussyfoot maneuver!

120
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:51,400
How insulting.

121
00:07:55,060 --> 00:07:59,200
It would appear that you need a
lesson in what real pirates are like.

122
00:08:01,020 --> 00:08:02,440
It's not pleasant.

123
00:08:02,980 --> 00:08:05,740
Your first lesson will be about terror.

124
00:08:06,320 --> 00:08:09,440
A lesson I learned well
as I stared down death.

125
00:08:14,600 --> 00:08:17,000
Hey, should he be in that stance?

126
00:08:17,280 --> 00:08:18,760
No, this is bad!

127
00:08:19,300 --> 00:08:21,124
Why is he using that technique?

128
00:08:21,520 --> 00:08:23,200
He's only fighting one guy.

129
00:08:23,560 --> 00:08:26,619
There's no reason to use
the out-of-the-back attack!

130
00:08:28,080 --> 00:08:29,920
This isn't a good spot for us.

131
00:08:30,060 --> 00:08:31,397
I mean, he can get us, too.

132
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:34,598
Yeah, he did say he was
going to kill us all earlier.

133
00:08:35,140 --> 00:08:38,081
Please, Captain Kaido,
anything but that technique!

134
00:08:38,360 --> 00:08:39,948
We'll do anything, Captain!

135
00:08:40,460 --> 00:08:42,040
Please, Captain Kaido!

136
00:08:42,580 --> 00:08:44,220
What's the big deal?

137
00:08:44,720 --> 00:08:47,020
He's just wobbling back and forth.

138
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:51,520
Out of the back attack!

139
00:09:01,820 --> 00:09:03,580
What a small haul!

140
00:09:04,360 --> 00:09:08,066
You know, I really thought they'd
have more treasure than this.

141
00:09:08,760 --> 00:09:11,819
Let's see if the boy hasn't
finished this fight yet.

142
00:09:13,880 --> 00:09:14,710
What?

143
00:09:14,793 --> 00:09:15,675
Everyone has stopped.

144
00:09:16,120 --> 00:09:17,060
Is it over?

145
00:09:28,900 --> 00:09:30,560
What's he doing over there?

146
00:09:36,020 --> 00:09:37,314
That guy's everywhere!

147
00:09:43,460 --> 00:09:46,620
Don't do this, Captain!
Please stop! We're dead!

148
00:09:46,980 --> 00:09:49,077
We can't reason with the
doubt that he's started!

149
00:09:49,160 --> 00:09:53,336
His sidestead maneuver is so fast,
not even he knows what he's cutting!

150
00:09:53,560 --> 00:09:56,972
But how could he have killed
so many of us without even...

151
00:09:57,140 --> 00:09:57,970
No!

152
00:10:03,540 --> 00:10:05,400
What's happening out there?

153
00:10:05,680 --> 00:10:07,980
People are just getting cut to ribbons!

154
00:10:22,920 --> 00:10:24,480
Shoo yourself!

155
00:10:25,500 --> 00:10:26,460
Butler!

156
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:40,720
Don't you have any honor?

157
00:10:40,900 --> 00:10:43,100
Those men are your friends!

158
00:10:46,340 --> 00:10:47,170
Reef.

159
00:11:12,860 --> 00:11:14,360
I found you!

160
00:11:15,380 --> 00:11:16,580
You bastard.

161
00:11:16,960 --> 00:11:19,797
You should have accepted
your fate like a good boy.

162
00:11:19,880 --> 00:11:21,409
Now look what you've done.

163
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:24,760
Thanks to you, my little
pawns are still alive.

164
00:11:24,980 --> 00:11:26,117
And in misery.

165
00:11:26,200 --> 00:11:30,080
it would have been better just
to let them die in the attack.

166
00:11:33,300 --> 00:11:34,740
So now what?

167
00:11:35,120 --> 00:11:37,740
Do you have something to say? Yeah.

168
00:11:38,220 --> 00:11:40,220
No matter what happens to me.

169
00:11:41,780 --> 00:11:44,000
I will never be like you.

170
00:11:44,260 --> 00:11:45,300
Not will.

171
00:11:47,980 --> 00:11:51,180
Someone like you can't be like me.

172
00:11:53,960 --> 00:11:55,040
You see?

173
00:11:56,200 --> 00:11:58,440
You are going to die here today.

174
00:11:59,760 --> 00:12:01,460
There's no need for that.

175
00:12:02,080 --> 00:12:03,845
Please, leave the children be.

176
00:12:04,080 --> 00:12:05,300
I'll write the will.

177
00:12:06,520 --> 00:12:07,840
No! Kaya!

178
00:12:08,140 --> 00:12:11,140
He's gonna kill you as soon
as you write that will!

179
00:12:11,980 --> 00:12:12,940
Silly girl.

180
00:12:13,420 --> 00:12:15,577
Don't you know you can't bargain with me?

181
00:12:15,660 --> 00:12:19,366
Captain Kuro specifically instructed
me to get rid of everyone.

182
00:12:19,700 --> 00:12:20,530
No!

183
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:31,997
If you don't do exactly as I say,
then you won't get to kill me!

184
00:12:32,080 --> 00:12:36,040
Ant, I won't write my will! Hold
on! Hold on! Just calm down!

185
00:12:36,260 --> 00:12:37,319
Don't be so hasty!

186
00:12:37,480 --> 00:12:40,304
I absolutely have to get
you to write that will!

187
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:42,900
Stop! Kaya!

188
00:12:45,640 --> 00:12:48,077
Alright, fine, I'll let
the little brats go.

189
00:12:48,160 --> 00:12:52,160
But in their condition, they won't
be making too quick of a getaway.

190
00:12:55,400 --> 00:12:57,857
Don't forget to sign your name I know

191
00:12:57,940 --> 00:13:03,917
I leave my entire

192
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:05,277
fortune to my butler.

193
00:13:05,360 --> 00:13:09,477
Clad or yes very good this is your

194
00:13:09,560 --> 00:13:13,117
wheel all right excellent work now.

195
00:13:13,200 --> 00:13:15,437
Remember we had a deal you promised me

196
00:13:15,520 --> 00:13:20,177
you wouldn't kill them
just relax I know I.

197
00:13:20,260 --> 00:13:23,672
I may not look like it, but
I'm regarded as an honest man.

198
00:13:23,960 --> 00:13:24,790
Kaya!

199
00:13:26,580 --> 00:13:27,410
There!

200
00:13:28,120 --> 00:13:28,950
Step on it!

201
00:13:29,033 --> 00:13:29,863
Go, go, go!

202
00:13:29,946 --> 00:13:30,776
Come on!

203
00:13:30,859 --> 00:13:31,689
Go, go, go!

204
00:13:31,772 --> 00:13:32,602
Let's go!

205
00:13:32,685 --> 00:13:33,515
Let's go!

206
00:13:33,598 --> 00:13:34,428
Let's go!

207
00:13:34,511 --> 00:13:35,341
Let's go! Over there!

208
00:13:35,500 --> 00:13:36,735
I can't help him out!

209
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:39,657
That's enough of that hypno-freak!

210
00:13:39,740 --> 00:13:41,280
Let the girl go! Damn it!

211
00:13:41,400 --> 00:13:42,929
Looks like I was followed.

212
00:13:49,520 --> 00:13:52,932
I guess I'd better finish off
the rich girl quickly, then.

213
00:13:58,600 --> 00:14:00,180
That was simply a war.

214
00:14:02,080 --> 00:14:04,340
The real fight begins now.

215
00:14:05,980 --> 00:14:10,960
Soon I will be feasting on your feet,
complimented by the sweet wine of your agony.

216
00:14:14,240 --> 00:14:15,070
Now!

217
00:14:16,300 --> 00:14:17,800
Out of the back attack!

218
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:39,980
Nice try, you jerk! Damn you!

219
00:14:40,160 --> 00:14:41,017
Get away from me!

220
00:14:41,100 --> 00:14:44,160
Wow, Butler man, right now
your life really sucks.

221
00:14:44,300 --> 00:14:46,757
Your plan of three years is
a complete and total failure.

222
00:14:46,840 --> 00:14:47,670
Let go!

223
00:14:47,753 --> 00:14:50,157
Hey, look, that weird
kid called Captain Kuro.

224
00:14:50,240 --> 00:14:51,257
I don't believe it.

225
00:14:51,340 --> 00:14:53,377
If that goofy kid manages to beat him,

226
00:14:53,460 --> 00:14:57,342
then that means Captain Kuro won't
be able to slaughter us, right?

227
00:14:58,080 --> 00:14:59,300
It's time to die.

228
00:15:00,720 --> 00:15:02,380
Oh, no, you don't!

229
00:15:08,920 --> 00:15:10,600
Stupid snot-nosed brat!

230
00:15:12,960 --> 00:15:13,790
Ha!

231
00:15:13,873 --> 00:15:16,197
Looks like you're one
step too late, swordsman!

232
00:15:16,280 --> 00:15:17,339
Wouldn't say that!

233
00:15:21,100 --> 00:15:21,930
Excellent!

234
00:15:22,013 --> 00:15:24,666
That branch was getting
in the way of my shot!

235
00:15:25,180 --> 00:15:26,010
What?

236
00:15:26,140 --> 00:15:27,460
Help me, Usopp!

237
00:15:27,780 --> 00:15:28,860
Do it, Captain!

238
00:15:30,400 --> 00:15:32,300
Eat this, hypnotist!

239
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:33,830
Yeah!

240
00:15:33,913 --> 00:15:35,037
Get him, you crazy rubber guy!

241
00:15:35,120 --> 00:15:37,238
You're going dead, you mean bastard!

242
00:15:37,360 --> 00:15:38,500
Get off me!

243
00:15:39,940 --> 00:15:41,080
Shut up!

244
00:15:41,300 --> 00:15:44,000
You have no right to cheer me on!

245
00:15:44,660 --> 00:15:45,780
Let go of me!

246
00:15:49,920 --> 00:15:52,360
Now, time for the exploding star!

247
00:15:55,400 --> 00:15:56,960
You insect!

248
00:15:57,480 --> 00:16:02,280
My spirit will absolutely
not be disrupted!

249
00:16:13,700 --> 00:16:17,297
As a kid, I never stopped.

250
00:16:17,380 --> 00:16:19,877
Searching for a great treasure!

251
00:16:19,960 --> 00:16:24,637
I had a map in my mind.

252
00:16:24,720 --> 00:16:27,277
That I knew would lead me!

253
00:16:27,360 --> 00:16:31,477
I had to find my way to that place.

254
00:16:31,560 --> 00:16:34,377
Before someone could beat me!

255
00:16:34,460 --> 00:16:38,557
The promised land was in my grasp.

256
00:16:38,640 --> 00:16:41,260
And I wouldn't let go!

257
00:16:42,040 --> 00:16:46,497
My only dream.

258
00:16:46,580 --> 00:16:51,617
I won't stop chasing

259
00:16:51,700 --> 00:16:54,440
it until it comes true!

260
00:16:56,040 --> 00:16:59,797
But if the world ever changes?

261
00:16:59,880 --> 00:17:02,957
I call out your name!

262
00:17:03,040 --> 00:17:09,817
We return to the time when
everything's the same!

263
00:17:09,900 --> 00:17:16,560
As long as I'm with you,
my memories won't fade.

264
00:17:17,340 --> 00:17:21,920
Waiting for that one true dream?
